MinGW compile fixes for the D3D shared-image pipeline enabled by 0021.

Two issues fall out of building d3d_image_backing.cc, dcomp_surface_image_backing.cc,
and dxgi_swap_chain_image_backing.cc with mingw-w64 ucrt64:

1) make_optional<gl::DCLayerOverlayImage>(size, comptr, ...)

   The DCLayerOverlayImage ctor takes Microsoft::WRL::ComPtr<IUnknown>
   (ui/gl/dc_layer_overlay_image.h). Call sites pass a derived
   ComPtr<IDCompositionSurface>/ComPtr<IDXGISwapChain1>/ComPtr<IDCompositionTexture>
   and rely on the WRL-provided converting copy ctor. With mingw-w64's
   wrl/client.h, that converting ctor isn't selected by std::is_constructible_v
   the way Microsoft's WRL does, so make_optional's SFINAE rejects every
   overload:

     no matching function for call to
     'make_optional<gl::DCLayerOverlayImage>(const gfx::Size&,
       Microsoft::WRL::ComPtr<IDCompositionSurface>&, uint64_t&)'
     ...
     no type named 'type' in 'struct std::enable_if<false,
       std::optional<gl::DCLayerOverlayImage> >'

   Fix: build a ComPtr<IUnknown> explicitly at each call site (the
   converting ctor IS available when invoked directly), construct the
   DCLayerOverlayImage by value, and let std::optional implicitly wrap it.

2) DCOMPOSITION_ERROR_SURFACE_BEING_RENDERED

   Used by dcomp_surface_image_backing.cc in a DCHECK. mingw-w64 ucrt64's
   dcomp.h does not define this HRESULT. Per MSDN it is 0x88760822. Define
   it conditionally in the only translation unit that references it.

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/chromium/gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/d3d_image_backing.cc b/src/3rdparty/chromium/gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/d3d_image_backing.cc
--- a/src/3rdparty/chromium/gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/d3d_image_backing.cc
+++ b/src/3rdparty/chromium/gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/d3d_image_backing.cc
@@ -1349,14 +1349,17 @@
 std::optional<gl::DCLayerOverlayImage>
 D3DImageBacking::GetDCLayerOverlayImage() {
   if (dcomp_texture_) {
-    return std::make_optional<gl::DCLayerOverlayImage>(
-        size(), dcomp_texture_, /*dcomp_surface_serial=*/0);
+    return gl::DCLayerOverlayImage(
+        size(), Microsoft::WRL::ComPtr<IUnknown>(dcomp_texture_),
+        /*dcomp_surface_serial=*/0);
   }
   if (swap_chain_) {
-    return std::make_optional<gl::DCLayerOverlayImage>(size(), swap_chain_);
+    return gl::DCLayerOverlayImage(
+        size(), Microsoft::WRL::ComPtr<IUnknown>(swap_chain_));
   }
-  return std::make_optional<gl::DCLayerOverlayImage>(size(), d3d11_texture_,
-                                                     array_slice_);
+  // d3d11_texture_ goes to the ID3D11Texture2D ctor overload; no IUnknown
+  // conversion needed.
+  return gl::DCLayerOverlayImage(size(), d3d11_texture_, array_slice_);
 }
 
 bool D3DImageBacking::HasStagingTextureForTesting() const {
